# Trivy ignore file for AegisGate Security Platform v3.3.0
# Format: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/v0.71/docs/suppression/
#
# Each line is an ID to suppress. To suppress a specific CVE/misconfig in a
# specific file, use: <ID>:<path> with # comment on the same or next line.
#
# See: legal-docs/21-self-attestation-v3.3.0/security-posture-v3.3.0.md
# Section 4.5 for the original review and remediation plan.

# === Secret findings: RSA private keys in upstream/aegisgate/ ===
#
# Status: ROTATED in v3.4.3 (OPSEC sweep #3, hotfix).
#
# Bug report confirmed that 3 RSA private keys were committed to public
# GitHub. Remediation steps:
#   1. Removed upstream/ from git tracking (commit 0a4b6a3)
#   2. Generated fresh test-only replacement keys and self-signed certs
#   3. Added *.key to .gitignore and specific path patterns for the 3 keys
#   4. Added .crt whitelist entries so self-signed test certs are tracked
#   5. Pre-commit hook blocks commits containing PRIVATE KEY string
#   6. Pre-commit hook blocks the 3 specific .key paths
#
# The upstream/ directory is RESTORED to git tracking because go.mod has
# replace directives pointing to ./upstream/aegisgate and ./upstream/aegisguard.
# Only the source code (.go, .mod, .sum, etc.) and test certs (.crt) are
# tracked. Private keys (.key) are gitignored.
#
# Important:
# - These private keys are FOR TEST USE ONLY. They MUST NOT be used to sign
#   production certificates, establish production TLS, or be deployed in
#   production environments.
# - The platform's runtime does not load these keys; they are only used by
#   Go unit tests in the adapters/tls packages.
# - The pre-commit hook in .githooks/pre-commit blocks any file containing
#   the string "PRIVATE KEY" from being committed.

# === Suppression policy (Rego) ===
# Trivy supports Rego-based suppression via --ignore-policy flag.
# This file documents WHY each finding is accepted as a known false positive
# for the v3.4.3 self-attestation. The actual suppression happens at CI
# runtime via the .trivy/rego/policy.rego file (not yet created; planned
# for v3.4.4).

# === golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp (CVE-2025-xxxx) ===
# Trivy flags golang.org/x/crypto as containing the deprecated/unmaintained
# openpgp sub-package. The platform does NOT import openpgp — we only use
# blake2b, chacha20poly1305, ed25519, pbkdf2, sha3, and ssh from x/crypto.
# The openpgp package is pulled in transitively but never called.
# This is a false positive for our usage.
# Affected paths: go.mod, upstream/aegisgate/go.mod, upstream/aegisguard/go.mod,
# usr/local/bin/aegisgate-platform (Docker binary).
# Code-scanning alerts: #405, #422, #424, #406.
CVE-2025-xxxx # golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp — not used, transitive only
